{"title":"Banyan Language Schools","sub":"Where will the value come from?","type":"Private equity","industry":"Education","geo":"Vietnam","diff":3,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Private equity value creation · operating leverage · EBITDA bridge","prompt":"A PE fund is buying Banyan, which runs 40 English-language schools for children in Vietnam. The price is 9× EBITDA, with debt of 4× EBITDA. The partner asks you to build the value-creation plan: how much could EBITDA grow in five years, from which levers, and what return would that give?","clarify":[{"q":"School economics?","a":"Each school has 600 places and is 70% full. Families pay $3,000 a year. Teaching materials and part-time tutors cost $600 per student; rent and core staff $700k per school a year."},{"q":"Levers?","a":"Management believes better marketing and timetabling can fill schools to 80%, fees can rise 5% with new digital homework tools, and 10 new schools can open in under-served cities."},{"q":"New schools?","a":"Each costs about $2M to open, paid from cash flow, and within three years reaches the same economics as an existing school after the improvements (80% full, fees 5% higher)."},{"q":"Debt at exit?","a":"About $30M."}],"structure":{"root":"How much value can the fund create at Banyan?","branches":[{"head":"Fill existing schools","items":["Utilisation 70% → 80%"]},{"head":"Charge more","items":["Fees +5%"]},{"head":"Open new schools","items":["10 schools","Capital needed"]},{"head":"Returns","items":["Exit value − debt vs equity in"]}]},"hypothesis":"Schools have high fixed costs, so each extra student is very profitable. I expect filling empty seats to be the biggest lever.","questions":[{"q":"What does one school earn today, and what is Banyan's EBITDA?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Students: 600 × 70% = 420. Each contributes $3,000 − $600 = $2,400: $1,008k. Less $700k fixed: <b>$308k</b> per school.</p> <p>Across 40 schools: <b>$12.3M</b> EBITDA.</p>"},{"q":"Build the EBITDA bridge to year 5.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"378.943281pt\" height=\"193.048pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 378.943281 193.048\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 193.048 L 378.943281 193.048 L 378.943281 0 L 0 0 L 0 193.048 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 25.783281 159.456 L 371.743281 159.456 L 371.743281 9.768 L 25.783281 9.768 L 25.783281 159.456 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"mff7d576334\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#mff7d576334\" x=\"62.020198\" y=\"159.456\" style=\"fill: #555555; stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #555555\" transform=\"translate(35.930823 174.184) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-f\" d=\"M 621 4659 Q 621 4749 698 4749 L 3571 4749 Q 3635 4749 3635 4678 L 3635 4352 Q 3635 4275 3552 4275 L 1318 4275 Q 1235 4275 1235 4198 L 1235 2701 Q 1235 2630 1306 2630 L 2963 2630 Q 3034 2630 3034 2560 L 3034 2221 Q 3034 2195 3021 2179 Q 3008 2163 2963 2163 L 1306 2163 Q 1235 2163 1235 2093 L 1235 538 Q 1235 474 1299 474 L 3648 474 Q 3718 474 3718 410 L 3718 70 Q 3718 38 3702 19 Q 3686 0 3648 0 L 710 0 Q 621 0 621 90 L 621 4659 L 621 4659 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-a\" d=\"M 698 0 Q 659 0 640 19 Q 621 38 621 77 L 621 4659 Q 621 4704 643 4726 Q 666 4749 704 4749 L 2182 4749 Q 3034 4749 3498 4435 Q 3962 4122 3962 3520 Q 3962 3136 3760 2870 Q 3558 2605 3123 2451 Q 3098 2445 3098 2425 Q 3098 2406 3123 2400 Q 3584 2285 3830 2006 Q 4077 1728 4077 1267 Q 4077 627 3597 313 Q 3117 0 2227 0 L 698 0 L 698 0 z\nM 2195 448 Q 2822 448 3129 649 Q 3437 